    "body": "Universal critical ASH* remains open for STACK and CLEAR separately. This session adds exact marked-input reciprocity and symmetric TWO insertion languages, four donor-one/two root identities, whole-history CLEAR escape/fuel restrictions, a componentwise conditional AS result retaining gap>=2, and distinguished-output occurrence symmetry. These are scoped tools; they do not establish global AS selection or threshold-preserving gluing.\n\nCold-challenged S01153-58 and replayed12 unchanged inherited checks. Three preregistered dual-validator campaigns pass:175359 configurations/16394311 exact relations;435 one-step barriers and78 fuel witnesses;42 critical transfers with literal donor histories and complete negative closures. Two fixed n6 controls have computed stack=clear8 and12. The zero-base draft failure and premature donor interpretation are retained and corrected. Historical hashes/cutoffs are unchanged.\n\nUpdated state/spec/catalogues/ledgers/audit/tool/workflow mirrors and complete strictly FUTURE/UNEXECUTED S013 handoff. Phase1 stays IN_PROGRESS; no Lean, registration, publication, correspondence or delegation.\n\nValidation: six new check-only replays, twelve inherited replays, all historical and90 new immutable hashes, governance and whitespace checks pass locally. Hosted results will be recorded from actual jobs; local success is not a universal/human/kernel or priority assurance.\n\nAtomic authored head: a201eeb0db60dfd68386ff76450a19ac4bb91c0a; tree5839db0ad2b4a4463d816a5accabbe25faa1745e; sole parent/base ca4aad7abf25d396eed16c6e3d89179ea6215b60. Ordinary PR; non-force two-parent merge only, no auto-merge. Actual jobs/merge/main reread will be recorded in integration metadata here.\n",
